Package: sparseDist
Title: Optimized Distance and Similarity Matrices for Sparse Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Gennaro",
           family = "Gambardella",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "gambardella@tigem.it",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7517-1347"))
Description: Computes column-wise distances, similarities, and memory-bounded
    k-nearest-neighbour searches for large, highly sparse data. Jaccard,
    Euclidean, Manhattan, Jensen-Shannon, Pearson correlation and covariance
    are supported, either among the columns of a single matrix or between the
    columns of two matrices. A full matrix needs memory quadratic in the number
    of columns, so a blocked search is also provided that returns only the k
    nearest neighbours of each column and never materialises the whole result.
    The kernels are written in C++ using 'RcppArmadillo', are parallelised with
    'OpenMP' where the compiler supports it, and report progress through
    'RcppProgress'. The Jaccard, Euclidean and Manhattan sparse kernels
    traverse only stored non-zero entries, so their pairwise cost depends on
    sparsity rather than on the full matrix dimensions.
